{"count": 1, "errors": [], "gaps": [{"id": "adr/ad-2026-01-15-thin-one", "type": "adr", "slug": "ad-2026-01-15-thin-one", "field": "body", "reason": "'## Decision' 4 words of prose, at least 15 asked for"}, {"id": "adr/ad-2026-01-15-thin-one", "type": "adr", "slug": "ad-2026-01-15-thin-one", "field": "body", "reason": "'## Decision' uses /\\b(tbd|to be decided|we should consider|still deciding)\\b/"}], "body": {"words": 55, "sections": [{"heading": "Context", "words": 30}, {"heading": "Decision", "words": 4}, {"heading": "Consequences", "words": 21}]}, "lenses": [{"code": "alternatives", "name": "A real alternative, not a strawman", "section": null, "instruction": "A decision with one option on the table is a description, not a decision. Name\nwhat else was genuinely considered and what it would have cost. If there was only\never one option, say that and say why \u2014 that is a constraint, and it belongs in\nContext."}, {"code": "consequences", "name": "The cost, not only the benefit", "section": null, "instruction": "Consequences that are all upside means the tradeoff has not been found yet. What\ngot harder? What can no longer be done cheaply? A reader six months from now is\nhere because something is painful and they want to know whether this record\npredicted it."}, {"code": "reversal", "name": "What would reverse this", "section": null, "instruction": "Name the observation that would make this the wrong call. Without it, nobody\nknows when to open a superseding record \u2014 and `supersedes` is the edge that makes\nthe history readable."}, {"code": "rule", "name": "A rule needs a requirement", "section": null, "instruction": "If this decision creates something the system must always or never do, that is a\n`requirement`, not a paragraph here. Add it and link it \u2014 `affects` carries the\nblast radius, and a rule buried in an ADR body is a rule nothing can check."}]}
